<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN" "task.dtd">
<task id="sessions-tabs">
  <title>Compare pages in tabs, windows, and sessions</title>
  <taskbody>
    <data name="doc-detective" value='test {"testId":"sessions-tabs","detectSteps":false,"runOn":[{"browsers":{"name":"firefox","headless":true},"browserFallback":"off"}]}'/>
    <steps>
      <step><cmd>Start at <xref href="http://localhost:8092/multi-tab.html" scope="external" format="html">the multi-tab page</xref>.</cmd>
        <info><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"goTo":"http://localhost:8092/multi-tab.html"}'/></info></step>
      <step><cmd>Click the Open child in new tab link. The child page opens in a new tab.</cmd>
        <info><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"click":"Open child in new tab"}'/></info></step>
      <step><cmd>In the newest tab, check that the page reads "PAGE linked".</cmd>
        <info><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"find":{"elementText":"PAGE linked","surface":{"browser":"firefox","tab":{"index":-1}}}}'/></info></step>
      <step><cmd>In a new tab named <codeph>report</codeph>, load <xref href="http://localhost:8092/multi-tab-child.html?page=report" scope="external" format="html">the report page</xref>. Then load <xref href="http://localhost:8092/multi-tab-child.html?page=scratch" scope="external" format="html">the scratch page</xref> in another new tab.</cmd>
        <info><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"goTo":{"url":"http://localhost:8092/multi-tab-child.html?page=report","newTab":{"name":"report"}}}'/><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"goTo":{"url":"http://localhost:8092/multi-tab-child.html?page=scratch","newTab":true}}'/></info></step>
      <step><cmd>Check that the <codeph>report</codeph> tab reads "PAGE report", and that the tab showing the scratch page reads "PAGE scratch".</cmd>
        <info><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"find":{"elementText":"PAGE report","surface":{"browser":"firefox","tab":"report"}}}'/><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"find":{"elementText":"PAGE scratch","surface":{"browser":"firefox","tab":{"url":"http://localhost:8092/multi-tab-child.html?page=scratch"}}}}'/></info></step>
      <step><cmd>In a new window named <codeph>settings</codeph>, with its first tab named <codeph>general</codeph>, load <xref href="http://localhost:8092/multi-tab-child.html?page=settings" scope="external" format="html">the settings page</xref>. Then load <xref href="http://localhost:8092/multi-tab-child.html?page=help" scope="external" format="html">the help page</xref> in another new window.</cmd>
        <info><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"goTo":{"url":"http://localhost:8092/multi-tab-child.html?page=settings","newWindow":{"name":"settings","tab":"general"}}}'/><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"goTo":{"url":"http://localhost:8092/multi-tab-child.html?page=help","newWindow":true}}'/></info></step>
      <step><cmd>Check that the <codeph>settings</codeph> window and its <codeph>general</codeph> tab read "PAGE settings", and that the newest window, titled "Child help", reads "PAGE help".</cmd>
        <info><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"find":{"elementText":"PAGE settings","surface":{"browser":"firefox","window":"settings"}}}'/><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"find":{"elementText":"PAGE settings","surface":{"browser":"firefox","window":{"name":"settings"},"tab":{"name":"general"}}}}'/><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"find":{"elementText":"PAGE help","surface":{"browser":"firefox","window":-1}}}'/><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"find":{"elementText":"PAGE help","surface":{"browser":"firefox","window":{"title":"Child help"}}}}'/><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"find":{"elementText":"PAGE help","surface":{"browser":"firefox","window":{"url":"http://localhost:8092/multi-tab-child.html?page=help"}}}}'/></info></step>
      <step><cmd>In the first window, check that the tab titled "Multi-tab home" still reads "MULTI-TAB HOME".</cmd>
        <info><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"find":{"elementText":"MULTI-TAB HOME","surface":{"browser":"firefox","window":{"index":0},"tab":{"title":"Multi-tab home"}}}}'/></info></step>
      <step><cmd>Type <codeph>hello</codeph> in the echo box of the help window, which is also the newest window, and of the child tab, the second tab opened.</cmd>
        <info><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"type":{"keys":"hello","selector":"#echo-input","surface":{"browser":"firefox","window":{"url":"http://localhost:8092/multi-tab-child.html?page=help"}}}}'/><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"type":{"keys":"hello","selector":"#echo-input","surface":{"browser":"firefox","window":-1}}}'/><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"type":{"keys":" again","selector":"#echo-input","surface":{"browser":"firefox","window":{"index":-1}}}}'/><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"type":{"keys":"hello","selector":"#echo-input","surface":{"browser":"firefox","tab":1}}}'/></info></step>
      <step><cmd>Load <xref href="http://localhost:8092/multi-tab-child.html?page=notes" scope="external" format="html">the notes page</xref> in a new tab named <codeph>notes</codeph>, and <xref href="http://localhost:8092/multi-tab-child.html?page=about" scope="external" format="html">the about page</xref> in a new window named <codeph>about</codeph>. Check that each one reads its page name.</cmd>
        <info><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"goTo":{"url":"http://localhost:8092/multi-tab-child.html?page=notes","newTab":"notes"}}'/><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"goTo":{"url":"http://localhost:8092/multi-tab-child.html?page=about","newWindow":"about"}}'/><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"find":{"elementText":"PAGE notes","surface":{"browser":"firefox","tab":"notes"}}}'/><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"find":{"elementText":"PAGE about","surface":{"browser":"firefox","window":"about"}}}'/></info></step>
      <step><cmd>Start two more Firefox sessions: <codeph>reviewer</codeph>, with an 800 by 600 viewport, and <codeph>editor</codeph>, with a 1024 by 768 window. Load <xref href="http://localhost:8092/multi-tab-child.html?page=review" scope="external" format="html">the review page</xref> in <codeph>reviewer</codeph>.</cmd>
        <info><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"startSurface":[{"browser":"firefox","name":"reviewer","headless":true,"viewport":{"width":800,"height":600}},{"browser":"firefox","name":"editor","headless":true,"size":{"width":1024,"height":768}}]}'/><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"goTo":{"url":"http://localhost:8092/multi-tab-child.html?page=review","surface":{"browser":"firefox","name":"reviewer"}}}'/></info></step>
      <step><cmd>In the first session, go back to <xref href="http://localhost:8092/multi-tab.html" scope="external" format="html">the multi-tab page</xref>, and check that it reads "MULTI-TAB HOME".</cmd>
        <info><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"goTo":{"url":"http://localhost:8092/multi-tab.html","surface":"firefox"}}'/><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"find":{"elementText":"MULTI-TAB HOME","surface":"firefox"}}'/></info></step>
      <step><cmd>Close the <codeph>report</codeph> and <codeph>notes</codeph> tabs, the scratch tab, the child tab, the help, <codeph>settings</codeph>, and <codeph>about</codeph> windows, and the <codeph>reviewer</codeph> and <codeph>editor</codeph> sessions.</cmd>
        <info><data name="doc-detective" value='step {"closeSurface":[{"browser":"firefox","tab":{"name":"report"}},{"browser":"firefox","tab":{"url":"http://localhost:8092/multi-tab-child.html?page=scratch"}},{"browser":"firefox","tab":{"index":1}},{"browser":"firefox","window":{"title":"Child help"}},{"browser":"firefox","window":{"name":"settings"}},{"browser":"firefox","tab":"notes"},{"browser":"firefox","window":"about"},{"browser":"firefox","name":"reviewer"},"editor"]}'/></info></step>
    </steps>
    <data name="doc-detective" value="test end"/>
  </taskbody>
</task>
